From 687d54560087950750a33752833470acce0a5a30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:51:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Generic interfaces: displacement gradient for finite strain
 behaviours

The caller may give the displacement gradient H = F - I instead of the
deformation gradient. This is selected at runtime: the stress measure,
K[1], is offset by 10. The behaviours which accept it export the
<function>_AcceptsDisplacementGradient symbol.

- Green-Lagrange strain framework: the strain is computed from H.
- Hencky strain framework: the logarithmic strain handler is built
  from F and from the Green-Lagrange strain computed from H.
- Behaviours written with F: they receive F = I + H.

This holds for the integration, the initialize functions and the
post-processings, for the generic and generic-parallel interfaces. In
plane stress, the axial component of H given by the caller is zero.
The MTest file generated on failure contains F = I + H.
